> Module Eitc

> Using Types
> Using Params_2024 as P
> Using Rounding as R
> Using Form_w2s as W

# Earned income credit (Form 1040 line 27)

Issue #26, `scope.md` section 6.2. Direct File ("DF" below) module
`../direct-file/direct-file/backend/src/main/resources/tax/eitc.xml`, read in
full. Law: 26 U.S.C. § 32 (`sources/statute/irc-32.html`); Rev. Proc. 2023-34
§ 3.06 (`sources/revproc/rp-23-34.pdf` pp 8 to 9); Pub. 596 (2024)
(`sources/pubs/p596--2024.pdf`); the Form 1040 instructions, "Earned Income
Credit (EIC)" Steps 1 to 5, EIC Worksheets A and B and the 2024 EIC Table
(`sources/forms-instructions/i1040gi--2024.pdf` pp 41 to 56).

The module has two scopes.

- `EitcTable` computes the credit for one set of figures (earned income, AGI,
  filing status class, number of qualifying children) exactly as the printed
  EIC Table does. It is the heart of the module.
- `EarnedIncomeCredit` decides whether the filer qualifies, computes the credit
  four times (without combat pay, with the primary filer's, with the spouse's,
  with both), picks the one the filer elected or the best one, and outputs
  `earned_income_credit`, Form 1040 line 27 (DF `/earnedIncomeCredit`).

Out of scope, as the issue says: Form 8862 Part V and the Schedule EIC PDF
facts. Per-person tests (is this person an EITC qualifying child, does the
child have a valid SSN) belong to the household modules (#16 to #18); this
module takes the two counts they produce as inputs (see "Inputs").

## The table emulation (the "$50 row midpoint")

IRC 32(f)(1): "The amount of the credit allowed by this section shall be
determined under tables prescribed by the Secretary." IRC 32(f)(2): "The
tables prescribed under paragraph (1) shall reflect the provisions of
subsections (a) and (b) and shall have income brackets of not greater than $50
each". The Form 1040 instructions say (EIC Worksheet A, line 4, and the
caption of the table) "Look up the amount on line 4 in the EIC Table to find
your credit". The table rows read "At least X, but less than X + 50", and the
credit printed in a row is the formula evaluated at the middle of the row.
Direct File reproduces that with

- `StepwiseMultiply(income, 50/50) + 25` for the income used
  (`/eitcRoundedEarnedIncomeWithoutCombatPay`, `/eitcRoundedAGI`): the bottom
  of the row (`income` with the cents dropped, divided by 50 with integer
  division, times 50) plus 25;
- a row that reaches the maximum credit at its last whole dollar (`row middle
  + 24`, because a row `[X, X + 50)` ends at `X + 49`) shows the maximum credit
  (`/eitcAmountWithoutCombatPay`, the `+ 24` case): this is how the row
  containing the end of the phase-in, for example 12,350 to 12,400 for one
  child, prints $4,213 although the midpoint 12,375 would give $4,208;
- in the phase-out, the income used is capped at the middle of the last row,
  `(bottom of the row of the completed phaseout amount + completed phaseout
  amount) / 2` (`/eitcPhaseoutAmountLowerBound`), because the last row ends
  at the completed phaseout amount and not at a multiple of 50 (the rows
  18,550 to 18,600 print $2, not $0, for no children: the credit stops at
  18,591);
- a phase-out is applied only if the row middle is at least the threshold
  plus 25 (`/maxEitcFromAGI`, `/eitcAmountWithoutCombatPay`: "If the
  threshold is greater than the lower bound of the row, we don't apply any
  phaseout").

All of this is checked against the printed table: `scripts/derive_eic_table.py`
parses the 1,337 rows of pp 46 to 56 of the instructions into
`sources/forms-instructions/derived-eic-table-2024.csv` (derived, not an IRS
file), and `catala/tests/test_eitc_table_golden.catala_en` (generated by
`scripts/gen_eitc_golden_tests.py`) runs `EitcTable` at the lowest and highest
whole dollar of every row for all eight printed columns (21,392 evaluations,
those at or above a column's completed phaseout amount not compared).
It also checks the second rule of Worksheet B: the credit is the smaller of
the credit looked up by earned income and the credit looked up by AGI.

Arithmetic: all intermediate figures are `decimal` (exact), and the result is
rounded once, to the dollar, half away from zero. Direct File multiplies
`Dollar` by `Rational` at two decimals with `HALF_EVEN` and rounds each
product; that is an engine artefact (CONVENTIONS section 8, Q10 and Q-R2), and
the exact evaluation is the one that equals the printed table on every row
(the golden test).

## Declarations

```catala-metadata
## Dollars as an exact decimal, for arithmetic that must not round to the cent.
declaration dollars content decimal depends on amount content money equals
  amount / $1

## The part of the credit taken back by the phase-out for income
## `rounded_income` (an already rounded row middle). IRC 32(a)(2)(B): "the
## phaseout percentage of so much of the adjusted gross income (or, if
## greater, the earned income) of the taxpayer for the taxable year as exceeds
## the phaseout amount". DF: `/maxEitcFromAGI` and the subtrahend of
## `/eitcAmountWithoutCombatPay` (the same switch twice). No reduction when the
## row middle is below the threshold plus $25; the income is capped at the
## middle of the last row, `(lower bound of the completed phaseout amount's row
## + completed phaseout amount) / 2`.
declaration phaseout_reduction content decimal
  depends on
    rounded_income content money,
    threshold content money,
    completed content money,
    percentage content decimal
  equals
    let last_row_bottom equals
      R.stepwise_multiply of completed, P.eitc_table_row_width,
        P.eitc_table_row_width in
    let cap equals ((dollars of last_row_bottom) + (dollars of completed)) / 2.0 in
    let income equals dollars of rounded_income in
    if threshold + P.eitc_table_row_midpoint > rounded_income
    then 0.0
    else percentage *
         ((if income < cap then income else cap) - (dollars of threshold))

## One calculation of the credit from the EIC Table.
declaration scope EitcTable:
  ## The earned income to look up (EIC Worksheet A line 4a, or with combat pay
  ## added). DF: `/employerIncomeSubtotal` or `/earnedIncomePlus...CombatPay`.
  input earned_income content money
  ## Adjusted gross income, Form 1040 line 11. DF: `/agi`.
  input agi content money
  ## Married filing jointly, which selects the joint thresholds. DF:
  ## `/isFilingStatusMFJ`; every other status (single, head of household,
  ## qualifying surviving spouse, and married filing separately under the
  ## separated-spouse rule) uses the other column.
  input is_mfj condition
  ## The qualifying children with a valid SSN, who count in the table. DF:
  ## `familyAndHousehold` `/numEitcDependentsCollectionForCalculation`.
  input qualifying_children content integer

  # The rates and amounts of the column (Rev. Proc. 2023-34 § 3.06(1))
  internal phase_in_rate content decimal
  internal phaseout_rate content decimal
  internal max_credit content money
  internal phaseout_threshold content money
  output completed_phaseout content money

  # DF: `/eitcRoundedEarnedIncomeWithoutCombatPay`
  output rounded_earned_income content money
  # DF: `/eitcRoundedAGI`
  output rounded_agi content money
  # The row reaches the maximum credit by its last whole dollar (the `+ 24`
  # case of DF `/eitcAmountWithoutCombatPay`)
  output row_reaches_max_credit condition
  # The credit that phase-in alone gives for the row, before the phase-out
  output phased_in_credit content decimal
  # DF: `/maxEitcFromAGI` (dollars, not rounded)
  output max_eitc_from_agi content decimal
  # DF: the `LesserOf` argument of `/eitcAmountWithoutCombatPay` that depends
  # on earned income (dollars, not rounded)
  output credit_from_earned_income content decimal
  # No credit at all: no earned income, or earned income or AGI at or above the
  # completed phaseout amount
  output no_credit condition
  # DF: `/eitcAmountWithoutCombatPay` (the same formula for each variant)
  output amount content money
```

The column of the table is chosen by the number of qualifying children
(0, 1, 2, "3 or more") and by joint or other filing status.

IRC 32(b)(1), `sources/statute/irc-32.html`: "In the case of an eligible
individual with: 1 qualifying child, the credit percentage is 34 and the
phaseout percentage is 15.98; 2 qualifying children, 40 and 21.06; 3 or more
qualifying children, 45 and 21.06; No qualifying children, 7.65 and 7.65."

```catala
scope EitcTable:
  # IRC 32(b)(1). DF: `/eitcPhaseInRate`
  definition phase_in_rate equals
    if qualifying_children = 0 then P.eitc_credit_percentage_0_children
    else if qualifying_children = 1 then P.eitc_credit_percentage_1_child
    else if qualifying_children = 2 then P.eitc_credit_percentage_2_children
    else P.eitc_credit_percentage_3_or_more_children

  # IRC 32(b)(1). DF: `/eitcPhaseOutRate`
  definition phaseout_rate equals
    if qualifying_children = 0 then P.eitc_phaseout_percentage_0_children
    else if qualifying_children = 1 then P.eitc_phaseout_percentage_1_child
    else P.eitc_phaseout_percentage_2_or_more_children

  # Rev. Proc. 2023-34 § 3.06(1) "Maximum Amount of Credit". DF:
  # `/eitcMaxCredit`
  definition max_credit equals
    if qualifying_children = 0 then P.eitc_max_credit_0_children
    else if qualifying_children = 1 then P.eitc_max_credit_1_child
    else if qualifying_children = 2 then P.eitc_max_credit_2_children
    else P.eitc_max_credit_3_or_more_children
```

IRC 32(b)(2)(B): "In the case of a joint return filed by an eligible
individual and such individual's spouse, the phaseout amount determined under
subparagraph (A) shall be increased by $5,000" (indexed). Rev. Proc. 2023-34
§ 3.06(1): "The threshold phaseout amounts and the completed phaseout amounts
shown in the table below for taxpayers with all other filing statuses also
apply to married taxpayers who are not filing a joint return and satisfy the
special rules for separated spouses in § 32(d)."

```catala
scope EitcTable:
  # Rev. Proc. 2023-34 § 3.06(1) "Threshold Phaseout Amount". DF:
  # `/eitcPhaseOutThreshold` (joint if MFJ; single, HoH, QSS and MFS otherwise)
  definition phaseout_threshold equals
    if is_mfj
    then (if qualifying_children = 0
          then P.eitc_phaseout_threshold_joint_0_children
          else P.eitc_phaseout_threshold_joint_1_or_more_children)
    else (if qualifying_children = 0
          then P.eitc_phaseout_threshold_other_0_children
          else P.eitc_phaseout_threshold_other_1_or_more_children)

  # Rev. Proc. 2023-34 § 3.06(1) "Completed Phaseout Amount". DF:
  # `/eitcCompletedPhaseoutAmount`
  definition completed_phaseout equals
    if is_mfj
    then (if qualifying_children = 0
          then P.eitc_completed_phaseout_joint_0_children
          else if qualifying_children = 1
          then P.eitc_completed_phaseout_joint_1_child
          else if qualifying_children = 2
          then P.eitc_completed_phaseout_joint_2_children
          else P.eitc_completed_phaseout_joint_3_or_more_children)
    else (if qualifying_children = 0
          then P.eitc_completed_phaseout_other_0_children
          else if qualifying_children = 1
          then P.eitc_completed_phaseout_other_1_child
          else if qualifying_children = 2
          then P.eitc_completed_phaseout_other_2_children
          else P.eitc_completed_phaseout_other_3_or_more_children)
```

IRC 32(a)(1): "In the case of an eligible individual, there shall be allowed as a
credit against the tax imposed by this subtitle for the taxable year an amount
equal to the credit percentage of so much of the taxpayer's earned income for
the taxable year as does not exceed the earned income amount." IRC 32(a)(2):
"The amount of the credit allowable to a taxpayer under paragraph (1) for any
taxable year shall not exceed the excess (if any) of— (A) the credit
percentage of the earned income amount, over (B) the phaseout percentage of so
much of the adjusted gross income (or, if greater, the earned income) of the
taxpayer for the taxable year as exceeds the phaseout amount."

So the credit is the smaller of `credit percentage * earned income` (capped at
the maximum credit, (A)) and `maximum credit - phase-out on the greater of AGI
and earned income`. Direct File writes it as the smaller of
`max - phase-out(AGI)` (`/maxEitcFromAGI`) and `phase-in(earned income) -
phase-out(earned income)`; the two agree with the statute in every case (the
phase-in ends below every threshold, so one of the two phase-outs is zero or
both income figures give the same phase-out). The EIC Worksheet B form of the
same rule: "If the amount on line 2 [AGI] is less than the threshold, look up
the earned income only; otherwise look up both and enter the smaller".

```catala
scope EitcTable:
  # DF: `/eitcRoundedEarnedIncomeWithoutCombatPay`: StepwiseMultiply(x, 50/50)
  # + 25, the middle of the $50 row of the EIC Table that contains `x`.
  definition rounded_earned_income equals
    R.stepwise_multiply of earned_income, P.eitc_table_row_width,
      P.eitc_table_row_width + P.eitc_table_row_midpoint

  # DF: `/eitcRoundedAGI`
  definition rounded_agi equals
    R.stepwise_multiply of agi, P.eitc_table_row_width,
      P.eitc_table_row_width + P.eitc_table_row_midpoint

  # DF: `/eitcAmountWithoutCombatPay`, first `Switch`: "If the upper band of
  # the row would exceed the max credit, use the max credit". The upper band of
  # the row is the middle plus $24.
  definition row_reaches_max_credit equals
    phase_in_rate * (dollars of (rounded_earned_income
                                 + P.eitc_table_row_last_dollar_offset))
    >= dollars of max_credit

  # IRC 32(a)(1) and (2)(A). DF: the minuend of `/eitcAmountWithoutCombatPay`
  definition phased_in_credit equals
    if row_reaches_max_credit then dollars of max_credit
    else (if phase_in_rate * (dollars of rounded_earned_income)
             < dollars of max_credit
          then phase_in_rate * (dollars of rounded_earned_income)
          else dollars of max_credit)

  # IRC 32(a)(2)(B). DF: `/maxEitcFromAGI`
  definition max_eitc_from_agi equals
    (dollars of max_credit)
    - phaseout_reduction of rounded_agi, phaseout_threshold,
        completed_phaseout, phaseout_rate

  # IRC 32(a)(2)(B). DF: the `Subtract` inside `/eitcAmountWithoutCombatPay`
  definition credit_from_earned_income equals
    phased_in_credit
    - phaseout_reduction of rounded_earned_income, phaseout_threshold,
        completed_phaseout, phaseout_rate
```

The statute gives no credit without earned income (the credit is a percentage
of earned income), and Rev. Proc. 2023-34 § 3.06(1) defines the completed
phaseout amount as "the amount of adjusted gross income (or, if greater,
earned income) at or above which no credit is allowed". Direct File's formula
does not stop there on its own: with earned income of $0 (for instance combat
pay only, not elected) the row middle $25 gives a credit of $2, and with
earned income plus elected combat pay above the completed phaseout amount the
capped last row gives $1 or $2. The table has no such rows (they print "can't
take the credit"), so the rule stands as the law says.

```catala
scope EitcTable:
  # DF-BUG(17): candidate. IRC 32(a), 32(b)(2); Rev. Proc. 2023-34 § 3.06(1).
  # DF has no zero case; see the text above.
  rule no_credit under condition
    earned_income <= $0
    or earned_income >= completed_phaseout
    or agi >= completed_phaseout
  consequence fulfilled

  # DF: `/eitcAmountWithoutCombatPay`: GreaterOf(0, Round(LesserOf(
  # /maxEitcFromAGI, ...))). The single rounding is half away from zero, as
  # DF's `Round`.
  definition amount equals
    if no_credit then $0
    else Money.max of $0,
      $1 * (round of (if max_eitc_from_agi < credit_from_earned_income
                      then max_eitc_from_agi
                      else credit_from_earned_income))
```

## Who is an eligible individual: the inputs

The inputs are explicit (CONVENTIONS sections 2 and 7), so that the
orchestrator can wire them from the modules that compute them. The wiring is
listed in the pull request: the Form 1040 slot `earned_income_credit`
(line 27) takes the output `earned_income_credit`; `agi`,
`employer_income_subtotal`, `interest_income` come from `Form1040`; the
filer facts from `Filers.Filers`; the combat pay from `Form_w2s.FormW2s`; the
two counts from the household modules.

```catala-metadata
## The answer to "Did the IRS ... how many years", DF
## `/eitcReceivedImproperClaimsNotice` with `/improperClaimsNoticeOptions`
## (`ctcOdc.xml` line 4): `twoYears`, `tenYears`, `zeroYears`. DF asks it only
## of a filer whose EITC was reduced or disallowed; `NotAnswered` stands for
## the fact being incomplete (no input is incomplete, CONVENTIONS section 3).
declaration enumeration ImproperClaimsNotice:
  -- TwoYears
  -- TenYears
  -- ZeroYears
  -- NotAnswered

## Form 1040 line 27 and its supporting facts.
declaration scope EarnedIncomeCredit:
  # ---- Return figures ----
  # DF: `/filingStatus`
  input filing_status content Types.FilingStatus
  # Form 1040 line 1z. DF: income.xml `/employerIncomeSubtotal`
  input employer_income_subtotal content money
  # Form 1040 line 11. DF: taxCalculations.xml `/agi`
  input agi content money
  # Form 1040 line 2a. DF: interest.xml `/taxExemptInterest`
  input tax_exempt_interest content money
  # Form 1040 line 2b. DF: interest.xml `/interestIncome`
  input interest_income content money
  # Form 1040 line 3b. DF: income.xml `/ordinaryDividends` (OUT OF SCOPE, $0)
  input ordinary_dividends content money
  # Form 1040 line 7. DF: income.xml `/capitalGainsOrLosses` (OUT OF SCOPE, $0)
  input capital_gains_or_losses content money

  # ---- Nontaxable combat pay (formW2s.xml) ----
  # DF: `/primaryFilerCombatPay` (Form_w2s `primary_filer_combat_pay`)
  input primary_filer_combat_pay content money
  # DF: `/MFJSpouseCombatPay` ($0 unless MFJ; Form_w2s `mfj_spouse_combat_pay`)
  input mfj_spouse_combat_pay content money
  # DF: `/allCombatPay` (Form_w2s `all_combat_pay`)
  input all_combat_pay content money
  # Whether the filer has answered the combat pay election. DF:
  # `IsComplete(/combatPayElection)`.
  input combat_pay_election_made condition
  # DF: `/combatPayElection`
  input combat_pay_election content W.CombatPayElection

  # ---- Children (familyAndHousehold.xml, #16 to #18) ----
  # DF: `/numEitcQualifyingChildren`: persons who pass the EITC qualifying
  # child tests
  input num_eitc_qualifying_children content integer
  # DF: `/numEitcDependentsCollectionForCalculation`: those of them with a
  # valid SSN, which are the ones counted in the table
  input num_eitc_qualifying_children_for_calculation content integer

  # ---- The filers (filers.xml, #15) ----
  # DF: `/isMarried`
  input is_married condition
  # DF: `/treatAsMFS`
  input treat_as_mfs condition
  # DF: `/specialRuleForSeparatedSpouses`
  input special_rule_for_separated_spouses condition
  # DF: `/treatFilersAsDependents`
  input treat_filers_as_dependents condition
  # DF: `/isMFJDependent`
  input is_mfj_dependent condition
  # DF: `/filersUSCitizenOrRAAllYear`
  input filers_us_citizen_or_ra_all_year condition
  # DF: `/filersHaveValidSSNsForEitc` (not in `Filers`: the SSN work-status
  # answers are not modelled there)
  input filers_have_valid_ssns_for_eitc condition
  # DF: `/primaryFiler/age25OrOlderForEitc`, `/primaryFiler/age64OrYoungerForEitc`
  input primary_filer_age25_or_older_for_eitc condition
  input primary_filer_age64_or_younger_for_eitc condition
  # DF: `/secondaryFiler/age25OrOlderForEitc`, `.../age64OrYoungerForEitc`
  input secondary_filer_age25_or_older_for_eitc condition
  input secondary_filer_age64_or_younger_for_eitc condition

  # ---- Writable answers of eitc.xml ----
  # DF: `/eitcQcOfAnother`
  input eitc_qc_of_another condition
  # DF: `/eitcQcOfAnotherRequiredToFile`
  input eitc_qc_of_another_required_to_file condition
  # DF: `/eitcQcOfAnotherIsFiling`
  input eitc_qc_of_another_is_filing condition
  # DF: `/eitcQcOfAnotherIsFilingRefundOnly`
  input eitc_qc_of_another_is_filing_refund_only condition
  # DF: `/eitcHadImproperClaims`
  input eitc_had_improper_claims condition
  # DF: `/eitcImproperClaimsDueToQc`
  input eitc_improper_claims_due_to_qc condition
  # DF: `/eitcImproperClaimTakenSinceDisallowal`
  input eitc_improper_claim_taken_since_disallowal condition
  # DF: `/eitcReceivedImproperClaimsNotice`
  input eitc_received_improper_claims_notice content ImproperClaimsNotice
  # DF: `/eitcImproperClaimsNoticeExpired`
  input eitc_improper_claims_notice_expired condition

  # ---- Sub-scopes: the four calculations ----
  without_combat_pay scope EitcTable
  with_primary_combat_pay scope EitcTable
  with_secondary_combat_pay scope EitcTable
  with_both_combat_pay scope EitcTable

  # ---- Filing status ----
  # DF: filingStatus.xml `/isFilingStatusMFJ`
  internal is_filing_status_mfj condition

  # ---- Earned income and the other money tests ----
  # DF: `/earnedIncomePlusPrimaryCombatPay`
  internal earned_income_plus_primary_combat_pay content money
  # DF: `/earnedIncomePlusSpouseCombatPay`
  internal earned_income_plus_spouse_combat_pay content money
  # DF: `/earnedIncomePlusBothTPCombatPay`
  internal earned_income_plus_both_tp_combat_pay content money
  # DF: income.xml `/earnedIncomeWithAllCombatPay`
  internal earned_income_with_all_combat_pay content money
  # DF: `/hasEarnedIncome`
  output has_earned_income condition
  # The completed phaseout amount of the return's column. DF:
  # `/eitcCompletedPhaseoutAmount`
  internal completed_phaseout_amount content money
  # DF: `/belowEitcEarnedIncomeLimit`
  output below_eitc_earned_income_limit condition
  # DF: `/belowEitcAgiLimit`
  output below_eitc_agi_limit condition
  # DF: `/belowEitcInvestmentIncomeLimit`
  output below_eitc_investment_income_limit condition

  # ---- Filers ----
  # DF: `/filersCouldQualifyForEitc`
  output filers_could_qualify_for_eitc condition
  # DF: `/filersAgeTestForEitcWithNoQC`
  output filers_age_test_for_eitc_with_no_qc condition
  # DF: `/hasZeroEitcQualifyingChildren`
  internal has_zero_eitc_qualifying_children condition

  # ---- Eligibility ----
  # DF: `/noEitcDueToSeparateFilingFromSpouse`
  output no_eitc_due_to_separate_filing_from_spouse condition
  # DF: `/maybeEligibleForEitcBase`
  output maybe_eligible_for_eitc_base condition
  # DF: `/maybeEligibleForEitcWithQc`
  output maybe_eligible_for_eitc_with_qc condition
  # DF: `/maybeEligibleForEitcWithoutQc`
  output maybe_eligible_for_eitc_without_qc condition
  # DF: `/maybeEligibleForEitc`
  output maybe_eligible_for_eitc condition
  # DF: `/eitcQcTest`
  output eitc_qc_test condition
  # DF: `/failsEitcQcTest`
  output fails_eitc_qc_test condition
  # DF: `/hasImproperClaimsAndNoQc`
  internal has_improper_claims_and_no_qc condition
  # DF: `/flowHasImproperClaimsAndAskAboutLastClaimedCredit`
  internal flow_has_improper_claims_and_ask_about_last_claimed_credit condition
  # DF: `/eitcNoticeTest`
  output eitc_notice_test condition
  # DF: `/eitcQualified`
  output eitc_qualified condition

  # ---- The four amounts ----
  # DF: `/eitcAmountWithoutCombatPay`
  output eitc_amount_without_combat_pay content money
  # DF: `/eitcAmountWithPrimaryCombatPay`
  output eitc_amount_with_primary_combat_pay content money
  # DF: `/eitcAmountWithSecondaryCombatPay`
  output eitc_amount_with_secondary_combat_pay content money
  # DF: `/eitcAmountWithBothTPCombatPay`
  output eitc_amount_with_both_tp_combat_pay content money

  # ---- Combat pay election ----
  # DF: formW2s.xml `/primaryFilerHasCombatPay`
  internal primary_filer_has_combat_pay condition
  # DF: formW2s.xml `/MFJSpouseHasCombatPay`
  internal mfj_spouse_has_combat_pay condition
  # DF: formW2s.xml `/someFilerHasCombatPay`
  internal some_filer_has_combat_pay condition
  # DF: formW2s.xml `/bothFilersHasCombatPay`
  internal both_filers_has_combat_pay condition
  # DF: formW2s.xml `/onlyPrimaryFilerHasCombatPay`
  internal only_primary_filer_has_combat_pay condition
  # DF: formW2s.xml `/onlyMFJSpouseHasCombatPay`
  internal only_mfj_spouse_has_combat_pay condition
  # DF: `/isEITCAmountWithPrimaryCombatPayGreaterThanWithoutCombatPay`
  internal primary_beats_without condition
  # DF: `/isEITCAmountWithSecondaryCombatPayGreaterThanWithoutCombatPay`
  internal secondary_beats_without condition
  # The largest of the four amounts, the right side of DF's
  # `/isEITCAmountWith...Maximum`
  internal largest_amount content money
  # DF: `/combatPayRecommendation`
  output combat_pay_recommendation content W.CombatPayElection
  # DF: `/combatPayElectionAndOrRecommendation`
  output combat_pay_election_and_or_recommendation content W.CombatPayElection

  # ---- Outputs ----
  # Form 1040 line 27. DF: `/earnedIncomeCredit`
  output earned_income_credit content money
  # DF: `/isReceivingEitc`
  output is_receiving_eitc condition
  # DF: `/eitc8862Required`
  output eitc8862_required condition
  # DF: `/receivingEitcWhileSeparatedCheckbox`
  output receiving_eitc_while_separated_checkbox condition

  # ---- Knockouts (CONVENTIONS section 6) ----
  # DF: `/claimedSpouseCombatPayWithoutMFJ` (BlockSubmissionOnTrue)
  output ko_claimed_spouse_combat_pay_without_mfj condition
  output unsupported condition
```

## Earned income

IRC 32(c)(2)(A): "The term "earned income" means— (i) wages, salaries, tips,
and other employee compensation, but only if such amounts are includible in
gross income for the taxable year, plus (ii) the amount of the taxpayer's net
earnings from self-employment". IRC 32(c)(2)(B)(vi): "a taxpayer may elect to
treat amounts excluded from gross income by reason of section 112 as earned
income." Section 112 is the combat zone exclusion: this is the nontaxable
combat pay of Pub. 596 (2024) pp 7 and 8 and of the Form 1040 instructions
("Combat pay, nontaxable", `i1040gi--2024.pdf` p 41): "You can elect to
include your nontaxable combat pay in earned income for the EIC. ... If you
are filing a joint return and both you and your spouse received nontaxable
combat pay, you can each make your own election."

DF takes Form 1040 line 1z as the earned income of the return
(`/employerIncomeSubtotal`: "Is used as earned income for calculating the EITC
and CDCC"). It computes the credit up to four times, one for each election:

1. no combat pay: earned income is line 1z;
2. the primary filer's combat pay added;
3. the spouse's (a joint return only: `/MFJSpouseCombatPay` is `$0`
   otherwise) added;
4. both added.

```catala
scope EarnedIncomeCredit:
  # DF: filingStatus.xml `/isFilingStatusMFJ`
  definition is_filing_status_mfj equals filing_status = MarriedFilingJointly

  # DF: `/earnedIncomePlusPrimaryCombatPay`
  definition earned_income_plus_primary_combat_pay equals
    primary_filer_combat_pay + employer_income_subtotal
  # DF: `/earnedIncomePlusSpouseCombatPay`
  definition earned_income_plus_spouse_combat_pay equals
    mfj_spouse_combat_pay + employer_income_subtotal
  # DF: `/earnedIncomePlusBothTPCombatPay`
  definition earned_income_plus_both_tp_combat_pay equals
    primary_filer_combat_pay + mfj_spouse_combat_pay + employer_income_subtotal

  # DF: income.xml `/earnedIncomeWithAllCombatPay`: Round(line 1z + all combat pay)
  definition earned_income_with_all_combat_pay equals
    R.round_dollar of (employer_income_subtotal + all_combat_pay)

  # Pub. 596 p 7: "to qualify, you must work and have earned income". The test
  # counts all combat pay, elected or not. DF: `/hasEarnedIncome`
  definition has_earned_income equals earned_income_with_all_combat_pay > $0
```

## The four calculations

Each calls `EitcTable` with its own earned income, the same AGI, and the
number of children with a valid SSN.

```catala
scope EarnedIncomeCredit:
  definition without_combat_pay.earned_income equals employer_income_subtotal
  definition without_combat_pay.agi equals agi
  definition without_combat_pay.is_mfj equals is_filing_status_mfj
  definition without_combat_pay.qualifying_children equals
    num_eitc_qualifying_children_for_calculation

  definition with_primary_combat_pay.earned_income equals
    earned_income_plus_primary_combat_pay
  definition with_primary_combat_pay.agi equals agi
  definition with_primary_combat_pay.is_mfj equals is_filing_status_mfj
  definition with_primary_combat_pay.qualifying_children equals
    num_eitc_qualifying_children_for_calculation

  definition with_secondary_combat_pay.earned_income equals
    earned_income_plus_spouse_combat_pay
  definition with_secondary_combat_pay.agi equals agi
  definition with_secondary_combat_pay.is_mfj equals is_filing_status_mfj
  definition with_secondary_combat_pay.qualifying_children equals
    num_eitc_qualifying_children_for_calculation

  definition with_both_combat_pay.earned_income equals
    earned_income_plus_both_tp_combat_pay
  definition with_both_combat_pay.agi equals agi
  definition with_both_combat_pay.is_mfj equals is_filing_status_mfj
  definition with_both_combat_pay.qualifying_children equals
    num_eitc_qualifying_children_for_calculation

  definition eitc_amount_without_combat_pay equals without_combat_pay.amount
  definition eitc_amount_with_primary_combat_pay equals
    with_primary_combat_pay.amount
  definition eitc_amount_with_secondary_combat_pay equals
    with_secondary_combat_pay.amount
  definition eitc_amount_with_both_tp_combat_pay equals
    with_both_combat_pay.amount
```

## Income limits

IRC 32(a)(2)(B) and Rev. Proc. 2023-34 § 3.06(1): the completed phaseout amount
is "the amount of adjusted gross income (or, if greater, earned income) at or
above which no credit is allowed". The Form 1040 instructions, EIC Step 2
(`i1040gi--2024.pdf` p 44): "No qualifying children who have valid SSNs, is
line 4b less than $18,591 ($25,511 if married filing jointly)?" and so on for
one, two, three or more children. DF tests earned income without combat pay
("We always test this without combat pay, since it will be the lesser of the
two amounts") and AGI, both strictly below the completed phaseout amount.

```catala
scope EarnedIncomeCredit:
  # Rev. Proc. 2023-34 § 3.06(1). DF: `/eitcCompletedPhaseoutAmount`; the same
  # figure as `without_combat_pay.completed_phaseout`
  definition completed_phaseout_amount equals
    without_combat_pay.completed_phaseout

  # DF: `/belowEitcEarnedIncomeLimit`
  definition below_eitc_earned_income_limit equals
    employer_income_subtotal < completed_phaseout_amount

  # DF: `/belowEitcAgiLimit`
  definition below_eitc_agi_limit equals agi < completed_phaseout_amount
```

IRC 32(i)(1): "No credit shall be allowed under subsection (a) for the taxable
year if the aggregate amount of disqualified income of the taxpayer for the
taxable year exceeds $10,000." Indexed (IRC 32(j)); Rev. Proc. 2023-34
§ 3.06(2): "For taxable years beginning in 2024, the earned income tax credit
is not allowed under § 32(i) if the aggregate amount of certain investment
income exceeds $11,600." IRC 32(i)(2): "disqualified income" means "(A)
interest or dividends to the extent includible in gross income for the taxable
year, (B) interest received or accrued during the taxable year which is exempt
from tax imposed by this chapter, (C) ... rents or royalties ..., (D) the
capital gain net income (as defined in section 1222) of the taxpayer for such
taxable year, and (E) ... passive activities". Pub. 596 (2024) p 6, Worksheet
1: line 1 Form 1040 line 2b, line 2 line 2a, line 3 line 3b, line 5 line 7 ("If
the amount on that line is a loss, enter -0-"). DF sums exactly those four
lines (`/belowEitcInvestmentIncomeLimit`, "The investment income from lines 2a,
2b, 3b, and 7 per 1040 instructions") and compares with the limit,
`<=` (the credit is lost only when the income "exceeds" $11,600). The other
items of Worksheet 1 (Form 8814, royalties, passive income) are not supported
income types in DF, so they are `$0` here.

```catala
scope EarnedIncomeCredit:
  # IRC 32(i); Rev. Proc. 2023-34 § 3.06(2); Pub 596 p 6 Worksheet 1.
  # DF: `/belowEitcInvestmentIncomeLimit`
  definition below_eitc_investment_income_limit equals
    tax_exempt_interest + interest_income + ordinary_dividends
    + Money.max of capital_gains_or_losses, $0
    <= P.eitc_investment_income_limit
```

## The filers

IRC 32(c)(1)(A)(ii)(II): "such individual (or, if the individual is married,
either the individual or the individual's spouse) has attained age 25 but not
attained age 65 before the close of the taxable year". This test applies only
to a filer with no qualifying child. DF's `/filersAgeTestForEitcWithNoQC`: for a
joint return either spouse may meet it, otherwise the primary filer must. The
ages come from `Filers` (`age25_or_older_for_eitc` and its pair, which already
follow Pub. 596's day-before-the-birthday rule).

IRC 32(c)(1)(A)(ii)(III): "such individual is not a dependent for whom a
deduction is allowable under section 151 to another taxpayer". IRC 32(c)(1)(C)
and (D): no credit to one who claims section 911 benefits or a nonresident
alien (the supported returns have neither). IRC 32(c)(1)(E) and (m): the
taxpayer's TIN, and the spouse's, must be a social security number issued by
the SSA on or before the due date (DF `/filersHaveValidSSNsForEitc`).

IRC 32(d)(1): "In the case of an individual who is married, this section shall
apply only if a joint return is filed for the taxable year under section 6013."
IRC 32(d)(2)(B): "An individual shall not be treated as married if such
individual— (i) is married ... and does not file a joint return for the taxable
year, (ii) resides with a qualifying child of the individual for more than
one-half of such taxable year, and (iii)(I) during the last 6 months of such
taxable year, does not have the same principal place of abode as the
individual's spouse, or (II) has a decree, instrument, or agreement ... and is
not a member of the same household with the individual's spouse by the end of
the taxable year." DF: a married filer who does not file jointly gets the credit
only if the separated-spouse special rule holds and the filer has a qualifying
child (`/noEitcDueToSeparateFilingFromSpouse`).

DF `/filersCouldQualifyForEitc` combines the filer-level requirements: the
return is not a joint return of two dependents (`/isMFJDependent`: "We ban an
MFJ dependent here, as they have opted not to take credits. A single person who
is a dependent may still be eligible for EITC with qualifying children"), both
filers are US citizens or resident aliens all year (IRC 32(c)(1)(D)), both have
valid SSNs, and a filer treated as married filing separately meets the special
rule.

```catala
scope EarnedIncomeCredit:
  # DF: `/hasZeroEitcQualifyingChildren`
  definition has_zero_eitc_qualifying_children equals
    num_eitc_qualifying_children = 0

  # IRC 32(c)(1)(A)(ii)(II). DF: `/filersAgeTestForEitcWithNoQC`
  definition filers_age_test_for_eitc_with_no_qc equals
    if is_filing_status_mfj
    then (primary_filer_age25_or_older_for_eitc
          and primary_filer_age64_or_younger_for_eitc)
         or (secondary_filer_age25_or_older_for_eitc
             and secondary_filer_age64_or_younger_for_eitc)
    else primary_filer_age25_or_older_for_eitc
         and primary_filer_age64_or_younger_for_eitc

  # IRC 32(c)(1), (d). DF: `/filersCouldQualifyForEitc`
  definition filers_could_qualify_for_eitc equals
    (not is_mfj_dependent)
    and filers_us_citizen_or_ra_all_year
    and filers_have_valid_ssns_for_eitc
    and (if treat_as_mfs then special_rule_for_separated_spouses else true)

  # IRC 32(d). DF: `/noEitcDueToSeparateFilingFromSpouse`
  definition no_eitc_due_to_separate_filing_from_spouse equals
    is_married
    and (not is_filing_status_mfj)
    and ((not special_rule_for_separated_spouses)
         or num_eitc_qualifying_children = 0)
```

## May the filer be eligible

IRC 32(c)(1)(A): "The term "eligible individual" means— (i) any individual who
has a qualifying child for the taxable year, or (ii) any other individual who
does not have a qualifying child for the taxable year, if— (I) such
individual's principal place of abode is in the United States for more than
one-half of such taxable year, (II) [the age test], and (III) such individual
is not a dependent for whom a deduction is allowable under section 151 to
another taxpayer". Every supported filer lived in the United States all year
(DF: "Due to scope, every TP and their spouse at this point has been a full
year US resident"), so (I) always holds.

```catala
scope EarnedIncomeCredit:
  # DF: `/maybeEligibleForEitcBase`
  definition maybe_eligible_for_eitc_base equals
    has_earned_income
    and below_eitc_earned_income_limit
    and below_eitc_agi_limit
    and below_eitc_investment_income_limit
    and filers_could_qualify_for_eitc

  # IRC 32(c)(1)(A)(i). DF: `/maybeEligibleForEitcWithQc`
  definition maybe_eligible_for_eitc_with_qc equals
    num_eitc_qualifying_children > 0

  # IRC 32(c)(1)(A)(ii). DF: `/maybeEligibleForEitcWithoutQc`. A married filer
  # must file jointly (IRC 32(d)(1)); the filer must not be a dependent.
  definition maybe_eligible_for_eitc_without_qc equals
    num_eitc_qualifying_children = 0
    and (is_filing_status_mfj or (not is_married))
    and (not treat_filers_as_dependents)
    and filers_age_test_for_eitc_with_no_qc

  # DF: `/maybeEligibleForEitc`
  definition maybe_eligible_for_eitc equals
    maybe_eligible_for_eitc_base
    and (not no_eitc_due_to_separate_filing_from_spouse)
    and (maybe_eligible_for_eitc_with_qc or maybe_eligible_for_eitc_without_qc)
```

## Qualifying child of another

IRC 32(c)(1)(B): "If an individual is the qualifying child of a taxpayer for
any taxable year of such taxpayer beginning in a calendar year, such
individual shall not be treated as an eligible individual for any taxable year
of such individual beginning in such calendar year." Pub. 596 Rule 10, and the
Form 1040 instructions, EIC Step 3 (`i1040gi--2024.pdf` pp 41 to 42): a filer
who is a qualifying child of another person cannot claim the credit, unless
the other person is not required to file and does not file, or files only to
claim a refund. DF takes the answers, not a second return (CONVENTIONS
section 8, Q6).

```catala
scope EarnedIncomeCredit:
  # DF: `/eitcQcTest`: the filer is not someone's qualifying child, or that
  # person is not required to file and either does not file or files only for
  # a refund.
  definition eitc_qc_test equals
    (not eitc_qc_of_another)
    or (eitc_qc_of_another
        and (not eitc_qc_of_another_required_to_file)
        and ((not eitc_qc_of_another_is_filing)
             or (eitc_qc_of_another_is_filing
                 and eitc_qc_of_another_is_filing_refund_only)))

  # DF: `/failsEitcQcTest` (Form 8862 Part II line 4)
  definition fails_eitc_qc_test equals not eitc_qc_test
```

## Improper claims

IRC 32(k)(1)(A): "No credit shall be allowed under this section for any
taxable year in the disallowance period." (B): the disallowance period is "(i)
the period of 10 taxable years after the most recent taxable year for which
there was a final determination that the taxpayer's claim of credit under this
section was due to fraud, and (ii) the period of 2 taxable years after the most
recent taxable year for which there was a final determination that the
taxpayer's claim of credit under this section was due to reckless or
intentional disregard of rules and regulations". IRC 32(k)(2): "In the case of
a taxpayer who is denied credit under this section for any taxable year as a
result of the deficiency procedures under subchapter B of chapter 63, no credit
shall be allowed under this section for any subsequent taxable year unless the
taxpayer provides such information as the Secretary may require to demonstrate
eligibility for such credit." That information is Form 8862, whose Part V is
out of scope (issue #26); the Form 8862 instructions (`i8862--2024.pdf`) say
Form 8862 is not required when the reduction was only for a math error or the
ban has run. DF's `/eitcNoticeTest` is true when any of the following holds:

- the filer has not had EITC reduced or disallowed;
- it was reduced because of a qualifying child, and the filer has no
  qualifying child now;
- the filer has claimed the credit again since the disallowal (the question is
  asked only when it matters, `/flowHasImproperClaimsAndAskAboutLastClaimedCredit`);
- the notice carried no ban (`zeroYears`);
- the ban has expired.

```catala
scope EarnedIncomeCredit:
  # DF: `/hasImproperClaimsAndNoQc`
  definition has_improper_claims_and_no_qc equals
    eitc_had_improper_claims and has_zero_eitc_qualifying_children

  # DF: `/flowHasImproperClaimsAndAskAboutLastClaimedCredit`
  definition flow_has_improper_claims_and_ask_about_last_claimed_credit equals
    (has_improper_claims_and_no_qc and (not eitc_improper_claims_due_to_qc))
    or (eitc_had_improper_claims and maybe_eligible_for_eitc_with_qc)

  # IRC 32(k). DF: `/eitcNoticeTest`
  definition eitc_notice_test equals
    (not eitc_had_improper_claims)
    or (has_improper_claims_and_no_qc and eitc_improper_claims_due_to_qc)
    or (flow_has_improper_claims_and_ask_about_last_claimed_credit
        and eitc_improper_claim_taken_since_disallowal)
    or (eitc_had_improper_claims
        and eitc_received_improper_claims_notice = ZeroYears)
    or (eitc_had_improper_claims and eitc_improper_claims_notice_expired)

  # DF: `/eitcQualified`
  definition eitc_qualified equals
    maybe_eligible_for_eitc and eitc_qc_test and eitc_notice_test
```

## The combat pay election and the recommendation

DF offers the election only among the options that apply (`/combatPayOptions`,
`constants.xml` lines 837 to 880), and when the filer has not chosen it
recommends the one with the largest credit (`/combatPayRecommendation`):

1. only the primary filer has combat pay, and the credit with it is at least
   the credit without: `usePrimaryCombatPay`;
2. only the spouse has combat pay, and the credit with it is at least the
   credit without: `useSpouseCombatPay`;
3. both have combat pay, and the credit with both is the largest of the four:
   `useBothCombatPay`;
4. both have combat pay, and the credit with the primary's alone is the
   largest: `usePrimaryNotSpouseCombatPay`;
5. both have combat pay, and the credit with the spouse's alone is the
   largest: `useSpouseNotPrimaryCombatPay`;
6. otherwise `noCombatPay`.

The election the filer made wins over the recommendation
(`/combatPayElectionAndOrRecommendation`). The variants only differ from the
no-combat-pay amount when someone has combat pay (`/someFilerHasCombatPay`).
The six constructors are those of `Form_w2s.CombatPayElection`, the same
enumeration as `Form1040.combat_pay_election`.

```catala
scope EarnedIncomeCredit:
  # DF: formW2s.xml `/primaryFilerHasCombatPay`
  definition primary_filer_has_combat_pay equals primary_filer_combat_pay > $0
  # DF: formW2s.xml `/MFJSpouseHasCombatPay`
  definition mfj_spouse_has_combat_pay equals mfj_spouse_combat_pay > $0
  # DF: formW2s.xml `/someFilerHasCombatPay`
  definition some_filer_has_combat_pay equals
    mfj_spouse_has_combat_pay or primary_filer_has_combat_pay
  # DF: formW2s.xml `/bothFilersHasCombatPay`
  definition both_filers_has_combat_pay equals
    mfj_spouse_has_combat_pay and primary_filer_has_combat_pay
  # DF: formW2s.xml `/onlyPrimaryFilerHasCombatPay`
  definition only_primary_filer_has_combat_pay equals
    primary_filer_has_combat_pay and (not mfj_spouse_has_combat_pay)
  # DF: formW2s.xml `/onlyMFJSpouseHasCombatPay`
  definition only_mfj_spouse_has_combat_pay equals
    mfj_spouse_has_combat_pay and (not primary_filer_has_combat_pay)

  # DF: `/isEITCAmountWithPrimaryCombatPayGreaterThanWithoutCombatPay`
  definition primary_beats_without equals
    only_primary_filer_has_combat_pay
    and eitc_amount_with_primary_combat_pay >= eitc_amount_without_combat_pay
  # DF: `/isEITCAmountWithSecondaryCombatPayGreaterThanWithoutCombatPay`
  definition secondary_beats_without equals
    only_mfj_spouse_has_combat_pay
    and eitc_amount_with_secondary_combat_pay >= eitc_amount_without_combat_pay

  definition largest_amount equals
    Money.max of
      (Money.max of eitc_amount_with_both_tp_combat_pay,
                    eitc_amount_with_primary_combat_pay),
      (Money.max of eitc_amount_with_secondary_combat_pay,
                    eitc_amount_without_combat_pay)

  # DF: `/combatPayRecommendation`
  definition combat_pay_recommendation equals
    if primary_beats_without then UsePrimaryCombatPay
    else if secondary_beats_without then UseSpouseCombatPay
    else if both_filers_has_combat_pay
            and largest_amount = eitc_amount_with_both_tp_combat_pay
    then UseBothCombatPay
    else if both_filers_has_combat_pay
            and largest_amount = eitc_amount_with_primary_combat_pay
    then UsePrimaryNotSpouseCombatPay
    else if both_filers_has_combat_pay
            and largest_amount = eitc_amount_with_secondary_combat_pay
    then UseSpouseNotPrimaryCombatPay
    else NoCombatPay

  # DF: `/combatPayElectionAndOrRecommendation`
  definition combat_pay_election_and_or_recommendation equals
    if combat_pay_election_made then combat_pay_election
    else combat_pay_recommendation
```

## Line 27

Form 1040 line 27 (`sources/forms-instructions/f1040--2024.pdf` p 2):
"27 Earned income credit (EIC)". Instructions: "If you qualify for the EIC,
... Enter the amount from the EIC Table or EIC Worksheet B."

```catala
scope EarnedIncomeCredit:
  # Form 1040 line 27. DF: `/earnedIncomeCredit`: zero unless qualified;
  # otherwise the amount of the election (or recommendation) that has combat
  # pay to count, and the no-combat-pay amount in all other cases.
  definition earned_income_credit equals
    if not eitc_qualified then $0
    else if some_filer_has_combat_pay
            and (combat_pay_election_and_or_recommendation
                 = UsePrimaryCombatPay
                 or combat_pay_election_and_or_recommendation
                    = UsePrimaryNotSpouseCombatPay)
    then eitc_amount_with_primary_combat_pay
    else if some_filer_has_combat_pay
            and (combat_pay_election_and_or_recommendation
                 = UseSpouseCombatPay
                 or combat_pay_election_and_or_recommendation
                    = UseSpouseNotPrimaryCombatPay)
    then eitc_amount_with_secondary_combat_pay
    else if some_filer_has_combat_pay
            and combat_pay_election_and_or_recommendation = UseBothCombatPay
    then eitc_amount_with_both_tp_combat_pay
    else eitc_amount_without_combat_pay

  # DF: `/isReceivingEitc`
  rule is_receiving_eitc under condition earned_income_credit > $0
  consequence fulfilled

  # DF: `/receivingEitcWhileSeparatedCheckbox` (the Schedule EIC / 1040 box for
  # a married filer who files apart under IRC 32(d)(2)(B))
  rule receiving_eitc_while_separated_checkbox under condition
    is_married and (not is_filing_status_mfj) and is_receiving_eitc
  consequence fulfilled
```

## Form 8862

Form 8862 is required to claim the credit after a disallowal (IRC 32(k)(2);
Form 8862 instructions). DF `/eitc8862Required`: the filer is claiming the
credit now (`/isReceivingEitc`), EITC was reduced or disallowed earlier in a
way that needs the form (`/flowHasImproperClaimsAndAskAboutLastClaimedCredit`),
the filer has not claimed it again since, and either the notice carried no ban
or the ban has expired. Part V of the form (the questions about
qualifying children not of the filer) is out of scope: this output only says
whether the form is needed.

```catala
scope EarnedIncomeCredit:
  # DF: `/eitc8862Required`
  rule eitc8862_required under condition
    flow_has_improper_claims_and_ask_about_last_claimed_credit
    and (not eitc_improper_claim_taken_since_disallowal)
    and (eitc_received_improper_claims_notice = ZeroYears
         or (eitc_received_improper_claims_notice != NotAnswered
             and eitc_improper_claims_notice_expired))
    and is_receiving_eitc
  consequence fulfilled
```

## Knockouts

DF `/claimedSpouseCombatPayWithoutMFJ` carries `BlockSubmissionOnTrue`: the
filer chose a combat pay option that refers to a spouse (`useSpouseCombatPay`
or `useBothCombatPay`) without filing jointly. The return is not supported
(CONVENTIONS section 6).

```catala
scope EarnedIncomeCredit:
  # DF: `/claimedSpouseCombatPayWithoutMFJ`
  rule ko_claimed_spouse_combat_pay_without_mfj under condition
    combat_pay_election_made
    and (not is_filing_status_mfj)
    and (combat_pay_election = UseSpouseCombatPay
         or combat_pay_election = UseBothCombatPay)
  consequence fulfilled

  rule unsupported under condition ko_claimed_spouse_combat_pay_without_mfj
  consequence fulfilled
